        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What lubricant does XTERRA recommend for its treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              XTERRA says to use only XTERRA Fitness approved lubricant. Each treadmill comes with one tube, and XTERRA says extra tubes can be ordered from XTERRA Sales. If you use another product out of warranty, choose 100% silicone treadmill lubricant, never a petroleum oil or WD-40, and check your manual.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How often should I lubricate my XTERRA treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              XTERRA's general rule is every 40 hours of use or three months, whichever comes first, but it tells owners to check the manual for their model. It gives the TRX3500 80 hours, and a TRX4500 manual we read gives 90 hours. XTERRA also suggests checking for lubricant every other month.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where do you put lubricant on an XTERRA treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On the deck under the belt, on both sides. XTERRA's method starts about a foot from the motor cover and lays a long S-shaped line about 4 to 6 inches in from each edge. Some manuals give their own distance; the TRX4500 manual we read says 18 inches from the motor cover.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I clear the LUBE message on an XTERRA treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              XTERRA's instructions say to hold the ENTER key for three seconds with the console in standby mode. Do it only after lubricating, so the next reminder counts from the right time.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do I need to loosen the belt to lubricate an XTERRA treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. XTERRA's method lifts the belt edge by hand far enough to reach under it. Long applicator tubes and wands make this easier. Because you do not loosen it, tension and tracking should be unchanged, but watch the belt for a few minutes afterwards.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much lubricant should I use on an XTERRA treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              XTERRA says half of its supplied tube on each side, which is one application. If you use a bottle that holds several applications, do not empty half the bottle; follow the bottle maker's dose, typically about half an ounce per side, or your manual's line length if it gives one.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

